    /*
     * Inline icon renderer, replacing <iconify-icon>.
     *
     * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     * WHY THIS EXISTS
     *
     * Icons across the feature cards, problem grid, module grid and checklists
     * were rendered as `<iconify-icon icon="ph:users-three-bold">`, a custom
     * element that only draws once a script from code.iconify.design has
     * loaded and upgraded it. Until then — and permanently if that CDN is
     * slow, blocked, offline, or the visitor is behind a strict CSP — the
     * element has no shadow root and paints NOTHING. There is no fallback and
     * no layout box, so the failure is silent: the card just looks like it was
     * built without an icon.
     *
     * These are inline SVG paths instead. No network, no custom element, no
     * upgrade step, and they inherit `currentColor` from the wrapper so the
     * existing plum/orange tinting keeps working untouched.
     * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     *
     * Keys are the Phosphor names already stored in the `icon` / `icon_key`
     * columns, so NO DATA MIGRATION IS NEEDED — the CMS keeps writing
     * `ph:shield-check-bold` and this map resolves it. The drawings are the
     * Heroicons outline equivalents, which match the SVG vocabulary the app
     * shell and sidebar already use.
     *
     * An unmapped key falls through to a neutral dot rather than rendering
     * nothing, so a future CMS entry with an unknown icon degrades visibly
     * instead of silently — the exact failure mode this component replaces.
     */
